Why the legacy build: the generic build calls Promise.try and Map.prototype.getOrInsertComputed
without a fallback, which older Safari on iPad lacks; the legacy build carries them.

Why no .wasm: the page's CSP has no 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (§3.4). pdf.js runs with useWasm: false
and decodes JPEG 2000 and JBIG2 with the JavaScript fallbacks above; ICC colour management (qcms)
is off. Scripting (quickjs) and the standard font data are not shipped: scripts never run, and
the browser's own fonts stand in for the standard 14.

The Web server serves only the files listed in STATIC_FILES (app.py); pdfpane.js loads pdf.js on
the first PDF opened. Updating PDF.js is a PR of its own: copy the new files, update this file.
